easywall (2.9.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Feat: the interface speaks French. locales/fr.json ships the whole
    interface — 463 strings — marked as unreviewed, because nobody who speaks
    French has read it yet; the language switcher says so beside the endonym,
    and so does the coverage report. That state had to exist before a
    contributed translation could
  * Feat: parity is now a rule for en and de alone. Every other language may
    have gaps: a missing key renders the English string, which go-i18n already
    did per message ID, and the gap is counted rather than hidden. Coverage
    never rounds up to 100, and declines to count an empty string or a value
    byte-identical to the English one, so the number cannot be raised by
    pasting
  * Feat: EASYWALL_CORE_* and EASYWALL_WEB_* — twelve variables, and the first
    environment either binary has ever read. The overlay runs inside
    LoadConfig, ahead of the Validate() call main already makes, so a malformed
    value from the environment is rejected exactly as one from the file is. The
    list stops at deployment: the environment configures where easywall runs,
    the interface configures what the firewall does
  * Change: the language switcher is a select with a submit button, not two
    chips. It still works with JavaScript switched off — an operator who cannot
    read the interface should not also need JavaScript to fix that
  * Fix: a malformed locales/status.json refused to start easywall-web. A
    syntax error in metadata about the documentation is now logged and read as
    "nothing is reviewed"
  * Fix: a wrapped tile label on the dashboard pushed its own number 20px below
    its neighbours. The tiles now take their four rows from the grid above
    them, at no cost to any language whose labels fit one line

