easywall (2.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Complete rewrite in Go (nftables via netlink, no Python dependency)
  * Two-process architecture: privileged core daemon + unprivileged web process
  * Direct nftables netlink API — no subprocess, no injection risk
  * Argon2id password hashing (replaces SHA512 with hostname salt)
  * Two-step activation with auto-rollback prevents SSH lockouts
  * Docker coexistence: own nftables table inet easywall
  * i18n: English and German
  * Light/Dark mode with OS preference detection
  * Export/Import rules as JSON
  * Auto-renewing self-signed TLS certificate
  * Debian package: only depends on nftables and openssl
  * logrotate config for audit log
  * CI: GitHub Actions, Dependabot, CodeQL, govulncheck

